From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paolo Pisati <paolo.pisati@canonical.com>
Date: Tue, 28 May 2024 06:27:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] UBUNTU: SAUCE: (lockdown) security: use default hook return
 value

Since upstream:

commit 260017f31a8c3879be5f9048a46f382b06c1923a
Author: Ondrej Mosnacek <omosnace@redhat.com>
Date:   Tue Jan 30 13:56:59 2024 +0100

    lsm: use default hook return value in call_int_hook()

it's not necessary to specify a default return value anymore.

Signed-off-by: Paolo Pisati <paolo.pisati@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00058
Ledger-Origin: ubuntu@f8e06f84b30449b9395368876ffa57f4d5aee216
---
 security/security.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/security/security.c b/security/security.c
index 0910b91c4639..afe99f16fc85 100644
--- a/security/security.c
+++ b/security/security.c
@@ -5580,7 +5580,7 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL(security_bdev_setintegrity);
 
 int security_lock_kernel_down(const char *where, enum lockdown_reason level)
 {
-	return call_int_hook(lock_kernel_down, 0, where, level);
+	return call_int_hook(lock_kernel_down, where, level);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(security_lock_kernel_down);
 
